    "_head_note": [
      "head_cy WAS 0.0518 AND PUT THE GLASSES ON HIS FOREHEAD (fixed 2026-08-13).",
      "",
      "This block is what the worn wardrobe aims at: draw_worn_glasses centres its lenses on",
      "head + (0, -0.06r) and draw_top_hat hangs its brim at head - 0.38r, so a head centre",
      "that is wrong moves every piece of gear by the same amount. Louis's backlog called the",
      "tailor 'drawn for the traced figure' and this is the whole of it.",
      "",
      "MEASURED OFF juggle_body.png, which is the only honest source: the crown is row 0, the",
      "chin is row 22, and the EYES are row 11 - visible as a dip in the skin-pixel count per",
      "row (9, 9, then 5 at row 11, then 9, 11, 14) because the dark eyes displace skin. The",
      "old 0.0518 put the head centre at row 8.5 and therefore the lenses at row 8.0, three art",
      "pixels above the eyes, which at ART_PIXEL 2 is six screen pixels - the difference between",
      "spectacles and a smear across the brow. 11/164 = 0.0671.",
      "",
      "head_r IS LEFT AT 0.0549 ON PURPOSE. It is doing a second job: the hat's brim is 1.5r to",
      "each side and the lenses span 2.1r, so r is scaling WIDTHS, and 0.0549*164 = 9.0 is the",
      "head's half-WIDTH (the skull measures 18 px across). The half-HEIGHT is 11, and using",
      "that would have widened the brim from 27 to 33 px on an 18 px head. One number cannot be",
      "both; the placement was the broken half."
    ],
    "head_cy": 0.0671,
    "head_r": 0.0549
  },
